{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.18","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":2822650}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"62b4803d","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Q-DBSCAN vs DBSCAN classique — APTOS 2019 (version corrigée et renforcée)\n\nCe notebook reprend `test-qdbscan-2` en implémentant les corrections proposées :\n\n| # | Changement | Où |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Validation croisée stratifiée répétée** + moyenne ± écart-type, test t corrigé de Nadeau-Bengio, test de McNemar exact, IC bootstrap | cellules *Expériences* et *Statistiques* |\n| 2 | **Plusieurs échelles d'angles** (`[0,π]`, `[0,π/2]`, `[0,π/4]`) pour traiter la périodicité du ZZFeatureMap + diagnostic de monotonie | cellules *Espaces de distance* et *Diagnostics* |\n| 3 | **Plus de données** (les 2930 images par défaut) et **plus de composantes** (4 et 8 qubits). La simulation exacte du ZZFeatureMap est vectorisée en numpy (vérifiée contre Qiskit) | *Configuration*, *Feature map* |\n| 4 | **Réduction supervisée (LDA)** en plus de la PCA, ajustée sur le train de chaque fold uniquement | *Espaces de distance* |\n| 5 | **Baselines** : k-NN et SVM-RBF classiques vs k-NN et QSVM quantiques, sur les mêmes features | *Expériences* |\n| 6 | **Part de prédictions passant par le repli k-NN** + précision du DBSCAN seul sur les points couverts | classe `DensityClassifierDBSCAN` |\n| 7 | **`eps` choisi sur un jeu de validation interne** (plus de fuite via l'auto-voisin), via un *percentile* de la k-distance, transférable d'un fold à l'autre. `MIN_SAMPLES` cohérent partout | *Classifieur* |\n\nTout ce qui est ajusté (scaler, PCA, LDA, MinMax, `eps`, `C`) l'est **uniquement sur le train du fold** (et sur un sous-ensemble interne du train pour le choix des hyper-paramètres).","metadata":{}},{"id":"dc439812","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 0. Installation","metadata":{}},{"id":"9dbb045c","cell_type":"code","source":"!pip install -q qiskit","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:16:56.350467Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:16:56.350973Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:17:03.96247Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:16:56.350936Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:17:03.960896Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":2},{"id":"443a927e","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Imports et configuration","metadata":{}},{"id":"53ea31bc","cell_type":"code","source":"import os, glob, time, copy, warnings\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport seaborn as sns\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\nfrom scipy import stats\n\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, RepeatedStratifiedKFold\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, MinMaxScaler\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\nfrom sklearn.discriminant_analysis import LinearDiscriminantAnalysis\nfrom sklearn.cluster import DBSCAN\nfrom sklearn.svm import SVC\nfrom sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, f1_score, cohen_kappa_score,\n                             adjusted_rand_score, normalized_mutual_info_score,\n                             pairwise_distances)\n\nimport qiskit\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import Statevector\ntry:\n    from qiskit.circuit.library import zz_feature_map\n    def build_zz_map(n_qubits, reps=1, prefix=\"x\"):\n        return zz_feature_map(feature_dimension=n_qubits, reps=reps, entanglement=\"linear\", parameter_prefix=prefix)\nexcept ImportError:\n    from qiskit.circuit.library import ZZFeatureMap\n    def build_zz_map(n_qubits, reps=1, prefix=\"x\"):\n        return ZZFeatureMap(feature_dimension=n_qubits, reps=reps, entanglement=\"linear\", parameter_prefix=prefix)\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n\n# ─────────────────────────── CONFIGURATION ───────────────────────────\nSEED        = 42\nN_SAMPLES   = 2930          # None = les 2930 images\nN_SPLITS    = 5             # folds de la validation croisée\nN_REPEATS   = 2             # répétitions (=> N_SPLITS*N_REPEATS évaluations par modèle)\n\n# (méthode de réduction, nombre de composantes = nombre de qubits)\nEXPERIMENTS = [(\"pca\", 4), (\"pca\", 8), (\"lda\", 4)]\n\n# Plage des angles après MinMaxScaler. Le ZZFeatureMap applique P(2x) : avec [0, π] la phase\n# couvre [0, 2π] et les deux bords du range se confondent (voir section Diagnostics).\nANGLE_MAXES = {\"π\": np.pi, \"π/2\": np.pi / 2, \"π/4\": np.pi / 4}\nREPS        = 1             # répétitions du ZZFeatureMap\n\nMIN_SAMPLES = 5             # DBSCAN (point lui-même compris) ; k-distance = distance au (MIN_SAMPLES-1)-ième voisin\nKNN_FALLBACK = 5            # k du repli k-NN pour les points hors densité\nQ_GRID      = np.arange(5, 100, 5)      # percentiles de la k-distance testés pour eps\nSVM_C_GRID  = [0.1, 1, 10, 100]\nNOISE_MAX   = 0.80          # on rejette un eps qui classe plus de 80 % des points en bruit\n\nTASKS = {\"binaire\": 2, \"multiclasse\": 5}\n\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\nprint(f\"Qiskit {qiskit.__version__}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:17:03.964292Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:17:03.964615Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:17:06.8519Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:17:03.964578Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:17:06.850591Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Qiskit 2.6.2\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"id":"aa6d42b7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Données APTOS 2019 (sous-échantillon stratifié)","metadata":{}},{"id":"ad245d95","cell_type":"code","source":"csv_matches = glob.glob(\"/kaggle/input/**/train_1.csv\", recursive=True)\nif not csv_matches:\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Ajoutez le dataset 'aptos2019-blindness-detection' dans votre Input Kaggle.\")\nCSV_PATH = csv_matches[0]\n\nIMG_DIR = \"/kaggle/input/datasets/mariaherrerot/aptos2019/train_images/train_images\"\nif not os.path.isdir(IMG_DIR):\n    alt = glob.glob(\"/kaggle/input/**/train_images\", recursive=True)\n    if alt:\n        IMG_DIR = alt[0]\n        if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, \"train_images\")):\n            IMG_DIR = os.path.join(IMG_DIR, \"train_images\")\n\ndf = pd.read_csv(CSV_PATH)\ndf[\"image_path\"] = df[\"id_code\"].apply(lambda x: os.path.join(IMG_DIR, f\"{x}.png\"))\nprint(f\"Total images APTOS 2019 : {len(df)}\")\nprint(df[\"diagnosis\"].value_counts().sort_index().to_string())\n\nif N_SAMPLES is None or N_SAMPLES >= len(df):\n    df_sub = df.copy()\nelse:\n    df_sub, _ = train_test_split(df, train_size=N_SAMPLES, stratify=df[\"diagnosis\"], random_state=SEED)\ndf_sub = df_sub.reset_index(drop=True)\nprint(f\"\\nImages retenues : {len(df_sub)}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:17:06.854136Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:17:06.85464Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:17:07.86787Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:17:06.854611Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:17:07.866791Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Total images APTOS 2019 : 2930\ndiagnosis\n0    1434\n1     300\n2     808\n3     154\n4     234\n\nImages retenues : 2930\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"id":"68386540","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Extraction des features ResNet50 (avec cache disque)","metadata":{}},{"id":"dae4bedf","cell_type":"code","source":"import torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\nfrom torchvision import models, transforms\n\nDEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\nCACHE_PATH = f\"/kaggle/working/aptos_resnet50_feats_{len(df_sub)}.npz\"\n\ndef preprocess_fundus_image(img_path, img_size=224):\n    img = cv2.imread(img_path)\n    if img is None:\n        return np.zeros((img_size, img_size, 3), dtype=np.uint8)\n    img = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n    gray = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2GRAY)\n    mask = gray > 7\n    if mask.any():\n        coords = np.argwhere(mask)\n        y0, x0 = coords.min(axis=0)\n        y1, x1 = coords.max(axis=0) + 1\n        img = img[y0:y1, x0:x1]\n    img = cv2.resize(img, (img_size, img_size))\n    lab = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2LAB)\n    l, a, b = cv2.split(lab)\n    clahe = cv2.createCLAHE(clipLimit=2.0, tileGridSize=(8, 8))\n    return cv2.cvtColor(cv2.merge((clahe.apply(l), a, b)), cv2.COLOR_LAB2RGB)\n\nclass APTOSDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, image_paths, transform=None):\n        self.image_paths, self.transform = image_paths, transform\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.image_paths)\n    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n        img = preprocess_fundus_image(self.image_paths[idx])\n        return self.transform(img) if self.transform else img\n\nids = df_sub[\"id_code\"].values.astype(str)\nX_raw = None\nif os.path.exists(CACHE_PATH):\n    cached = np.load(CACHE_PATH, allow_pickle=True)\n    if np.array_equal(cached[\"ids\"], ids):\n        X_raw = cached[\"X\"]\n        print(f\"Features rechargées depuis le cache : {X_raw.shape}\")\n\nif X_raw is None:\n    transform_resnet = transforms.Compose([\n        transforms.ToPILImage(), transforms.ToTensor(),\n        transforms.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),\n    ])\n    loader = DataLoader(APTOSDataset(df_sub[\"image_path\"].values, transform_resnet),\n                        batch_size=32, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n    resnet = models.resnet50(weights=models.ResNet50_Weights.DEFAULT)\n    resnet.fc = nn.Identity()\n    resnet = resnet.to(DEVICE).eval()\n    feats = []\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        for batch in tqdm(loader, desc=\"Extraction ResNet50\"):\n            feats.append(resnet(batch.to(DEVICE)).cpu().numpy())\n    X_raw = np.vstack(feats)\n    try:\n        np.savez_compressed(CACHE_PATH, X=X_raw, ids=ids)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"Cache non sauvegardé :\", e)\n\ny_multi = df_sub[\"diagnosis\"].values.astype(int)\ny_bin   = (y_multi > 0).astype(int)\nY = {\"binaire\": y_bin, \"multiclasse\": y_multi}\nprint(\"X_raw :\", X_raw.shape)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:17:07.869066Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:17:07.869427Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:27:10.249364Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:17:07.869401Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:27:10.247826Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Downloading: \"https://download.pytorch.org/models/resnet50-11ad3fa6.pth\" to /root/.cache/torch/hub/checkpoints/resnet50-11ad3fa6.pth\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stderr","text":"100%|██████████| 97.8M/97.8M [00:00<00:00, 163MB/s]\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Extraction ResNet50:   0%|          | 0/92 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"4055f813df6246e5af393deaf2258ce4"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"X_raw : (2930, 2048)\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"id":"5a4a00c7-e2a7-4a32-9ac8-8317140716dc","cell_type":"code","source":"img = cv2.imread(\"/kaggle/input/datasets/mariaherrerot/aptos2019/train_images/train_images/1b32e1d775ea.png\")\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(8, 5))\naxes[0].imshow(img)\naxes[0].set_title('avant pré-traitement')\naxes[1].imshow(preprocess_fundus_image(\"/kaggle/input/datasets/mariaherrerot/aptos2019/train_images/train_images/1b32e1d775ea.png\"))\naxes[1].set_title('après pré-traitement')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:27:10.252755Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:27:10.254231Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:27:21.186631Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:27:10.254169Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:27:21.184874Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 800x500 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"898d9261","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Simulation exacte du ZZFeatureMap\n\nLe circuit `ZZFeatureMap(reps=1, entanglement=\"linear\")` prépare l'état\n\n$$|\\psi(x)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\\sum_{z\\in\\{0,1\\}^n} e^{\\,i\\left[\\sum_i 2x_i z_i \\;+\\; \\sum_i 2(\\pi-x_i)(\\pi-x_{i+1})\\,(z_i\\oplus z_{i+1})\\right]}|z\\rangle$$\n\n(pour `reps>1` on intercale une transformée de Hadamard entre chaque couche de phases). On peut donc calculer tous les états d'un coup avec numpy, ce qui supprime le goulot d'étranglement du `Statevector` image par image. La cellule suivante **vérifie** l'équivalence avec Qiskit.","metadata":{}},{"id":"358e813f","cell_type":"code","source":"def _hadamard_matrix(n):\n    H1 = np.array([[1.0, 1.0], [1.0, -1.0]]) / np.sqrt(2)\n    H = np.array([[1.0]])\n    for _ in range(n):\n        H = np.kron(H, H1)\n    return H\n\n_BITS = {}\ndef _bits(n):\n    if n not in _BITS:\n        idx = np.arange(2 ** n)\n        _BITS[n] = ((idx[:, None] >> np.arange(n)) & 1).astype(np.float64)   # bit i = qubit i\n    return _BITS[n]\n\ndef zz_states(X, reps=1):\n    '''Vecteurs d'état (N, 2^n) du ZZFeatureMap (intrication linéaire), simulation exacte.'''\n    X = np.asarray(X, dtype=np.float64)\n    N, n = X.shape\n    bits = _bits(n)\n    phase = 2.0 * X @ bits.T\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        coef = 2.0 * (np.pi - X[:, i]) * (np.pi - X[:, i + 1])\n        parity = np.abs(bits[:, i] - bits[:, i + 1])\n        phase += coef[:, None] * parity[None, :]\n    U = np.exp(1j * phase)\n    H = _hadamard_matrix(n) if reps > 1 else None\n    psi = np.full((N, 2 ** n), 1.0 / np.sqrt(2 ** n), dtype=complex)\n    for r in range(reps):\n        psi = psi * U\n        if r < reps - 1:\n            psi = psi @ H\n    return psi\n\n# ── Vérification contre Qiskit ──\nrng = np.random.default_rng(0)\nfor n_q in (4, 8):\n    for reps in (1, 2):\n        Xc = rng.uniform(0, np.pi, size=(6, n_q))\n        fm = build_zz_map(n_q, reps)\n        params = list(fm.parameters)\n        sv = np.array([Statevector.from_instruction(fm.assign_parameters(dict(zip(params, x)))).data for x in Xc])\n        F_qiskit = np.abs(sv @ sv.conj().T) ** 2\n        P = zz_states(Xc, reps)\n        err = np.abs(F_qiskit - np.abs(P @ P.conj().T) ** 2).max()\n        assert err < 1e-9, f\"Écart numpy/Qiskit trop grand ({n_q} qubits, reps={reps}) : {err}\"\n        print(f\"{n_q} qubits, reps={reps} : écart max sur la fidélité = {err:.1e}  ✔\")\n\n# ── Circuit Compute-Uncompute (pour le rapport) ──\nfm_j = build_zz_map(4, reps=1, prefix=\"xj\")\nfm_i_inv = build_zz_map(4, reps=1, prefix=\"xi\").inverse()\nqc_demo = fm_j.compose(fm_i_inv)\nqc_demo.measure_all()\nprint(f\"\\nCircuit compute-uncompute : {qc_demo.num_qubits} qubits, profondeur {qc_demo.decompose().depth()}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:29:10.418077Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:29:10.418773Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:29:10.777496Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:29:10.418728Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:29:10.77625Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"4 qubits, reps=1 : écart max sur la fidélité = 1.8e-15  ✔\n4 qubits, reps=2 : écart max sur la fidélité = 2.4e-15  ✔\n8 qubits, reps=1 : écart max sur la fidélité = 3.1e-15  ✔\n8 qubits, reps=2 : écart max sur la fidélité = 4.0e-15  ✔\n\nCircuit compute-uncompute : 4 qubits, profondeur 23\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"id":"ecbb63c5","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Espaces de distance (réduction → angles → noyau quantique)\n\nPour chaque fold on construit, **uniquement à partir du train**, plusieurs « espaces » :\n\n* `Euclid` : distance euclidienne dans l'espace réduit (référence classique) ;\n* `Q π`, `Q π/2`, `Q π/4` : distance quantique $D=\\sqrt{1-F}$ avec $F=|\\langle\\psi(x)|\\psi(x')\\rangle|^2$, pour trois plages d'angles.\n\nPour LDA, la réduction est ajustée sur les labels **multiclasses** du train (au plus 4 composantes pour 5 classes) après une PCA à 64 dimensions pour éviter le sur-ajustement (2048 features ≫ échantillons).","metadata":{}},{"id":"54ef8c06","cell_type":"code","source":"def reduce_features(Xtr_raw, Xev_raw, ytr_multi, kind, n_comp, seed):\n    sc = StandardScaler().fit(Xtr_raw)\n    A, B = sc.transform(Xtr_raw), sc.transform(Xev_raw)\n    var = np.nan\n    if kind == \"pca\":\n        red = PCA(n_components=n_comp, random_state=seed).fit(A)\n        var = float(red.explained_variance_ratio_.sum())\n    elif kind == \"lda\":\n        pre = PCA(n_components=min(64, A.shape[0] - 1), random_state=seed).fit(A)\n        A, B = pre.transform(A), pre.transform(B)\n        n_lda = min(n_comp, len(np.unique(ytr_multi)) - 1)\n        red = LinearDiscriminantAnalysis(solver=\"eigen\", shrinkage=\"auto\", n_components=n_lda).fit(A, ytr_multi)\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(kind)\n    return red.transform(A), red.transform(B), var\n\ndef build_spaces(idx_tr, idx_ev, kind, n_comp, seed):\n    '''Retourne {nom: dict(D, Dev, K, Kev, Z, Zev)} ; tout est ajusté sur idx_tr uniquement.'''\n    Ztr, Zev, var = reduce_features(X_raw[idx_tr], X_raw[idx_ev], y_multi[idx_tr], kind, n_comp, seed)\n    spaces = {\"Euclid\": dict(D=pairwise_distances(Ztr), Dev=pairwise_distances(Zev, Ztr),\n                             K=None, Kev=None, Z=Ztr, Zev=Zev)}\n    for a_name, a_max in ANGLE_MAXES.items():\n        sc = MinMaxScaler(feature_range=(0, a_max)).fit(Ztr)\n        Atr = np.clip(sc.transform(Ztr), 0, a_max)\n        Aev = np.clip(sc.transform(Zev), 0, a_max)\n        Ptr, Pev = zz_states(Atr, REPS), zz_states(Aev, REPS)\n        K = np.clip(np.abs(Ptr @ Ptr.conj().T) ** 2, 0.0, 1.0)\n        Kev = np.clip(np.abs(Pev @ Ptr.conj().T) ** 2, 0.0, 1.0)\n        D = np.sqrt(1.0 - K)\n        np.fill_diagonal(D, 0.0)\n        spaces[f\"Q {a_name}\"] = dict(D=D, Dev=np.sqrt(1.0 - Kev), K=K, Kev=Kev, Z=Atr, Zev=Aev)\n    return spaces, var","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:29:14.378814Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:29:14.379225Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:29:14.394071Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:29:14.379196Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:29:14.392238Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":8},{"id":"ac06e96e","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6. Classifieurs\n\n**`DensityClassifierDBSCAN`** : on clusterise le train avec DBSCAN (distance pré-calculée), chaque cluster prend le label majoritaire. Un point à prédire hérite du cluster du core point le plus proche s'il est à moins de `eps`, sinon on **replie** sur un k-NN. La méthode `predict` renvoie aussi le masque `covered` (= prédiction par la densité, sans repli) pour mesurer ce que fait réellement le DBSCAN.\n\n**Choix de `eps`** : on tune un *percentile* $q$ de la k-distance (et non une valeur absolue, qui n'aurait pas le même sens d'un fold à l'autre) sur un **jeu de validation interne** (80/20 du train, tout refit sur la partie 80 %). Le clustering étant non supervisé, il est calculé une seule fois par $q$ puis réutilisé pour les deux tâches.","metadata":{}},{"id":"d9b50d93","cell_type":"code","source":"def kdist(D, min_samples=MIN_SAMPLES):\n    # colonne 0 = le point lui-même (distance 0) -> min_samples-ième point = colonne min_samples-1\n    return np.sort(D, axis=1)[:, min_samples - 1]\n\ndef vote(nn_idx, y, n_classes):\n    onehot = np.eye(n_classes, dtype=np.int32)[y]\n    return onehot[nn_idx].sum(axis=1).argmax(axis=1)\n\ndef knn_predict(D_ev, y_train, k, n_classes):\n    k = min(k, D_ev.shape[1])\n    nn_idx = np.argpartition(D_ev, k - 1, axis=1)[:, :k]\n    return vote(nn_idx, y_train, n_classes)\n\nclass DensityClassifierDBSCAN:\n    def __init__(self, eps, min_samples=MIN_SAMPLES, knn_fallback=KNN_FALLBACK):\n        self.eps, self.min_samples, self.knn_fallback = float(eps), min_samples, knn_fallback\n\n    def cluster(self, D_train):                      # non supervisé\n        db = DBSCAN(eps=self.eps, min_samples=self.min_samples, metric=\"precomputed\").fit(D_train)\n        self.labels_ = db.labels_\n        self.core_ = db.core_sample_indices_\n        self.n_clusters_ = len(set(self.labels_) - {-1})\n        self.noise_ratio_ = float(np.mean(self.labels_ == -1))\n        return self\n\n    def fit_labels(self, y_train, n_classes):        # supervisé : label majoritaire par cluster\n        self.y_train_, self.n_classes_ = np.asarray(y_train), n_classes\n        self.lut_ = np.zeros(max(self.n_clusters_, 1), dtype=int)\n        for c in range(self.n_clusters_):\n            self.lut_[c] = np.bincount(self.y_train_[self.labels_ == c], minlength=n_classes).argmax()\n        return self\n\n    def predict(self, D_ev):\n        m = D_ev.shape[0]\n        covered = np.zeros(m, dtype=bool)\n        pred_cov = np.zeros(m, dtype=int)\n        if len(self.core_) > 0 and self.n_clusters_ > 0:\n            Dc = D_ev[:, self.core_]\n            j = Dc.argmin(axis=1)\n            covered = Dc[np.arange(m), j] <= self.eps\n            pred_cov = self.lut_[self.labels_[self.core_[j]]]\n        pred_knn = knn_predict(D_ev, self.y_train_, self.knn_fallback, self.n_classes_)\n        return np.where(covered, pred_cov, pred_knn), covered\n\ndef tune_percentiles(D_fit, D_val, y_fit, y_val):\n    '''Choisit, pour chaque tâche, le percentile q de la k-distance maximisant le F1-macro de validation.'''\n    kd = kdist(D_fit)\n    best = {t: (-1.0, None) for t in TASKS}\n    for q in Q_GRID:\n        eps = float(np.percentile(kd, q))\n        if eps <= 0:\n            continue\n        clf = DensityClassifierDBSCAN(eps).cluster(D_fit)\n        if clf.n_clusters_ < 2 or clf.noise_ratio_ > NOISE_MAX:\n            continue\n        for t, C in TASKS.items():\n            pred, _ = copy.copy(clf).fit_labels(y_fit[t], C).predict(D_val)\n            s = f1_score(y_val[t], pred, average=\"macro\")\n            if s > best[t][0]:\n                best[t] = (s, q)\n    return {t: (best[t][1] if best[t][1] is not None else 50.0) for t in TASKS}\n\ndef svm_fit_predict(sp_tr, y_tr, sp_ev, C):\n    if sp_tr[\"K\"] is None:                           # SVM-RBF classique sur l'espace réduit\n        m = SVC(kernel=\"rbf\", gamma=\"scale\", C=C, class_weight=\"balanced\").fit(sp_tr[\"Z\"], y_tr)\n        return m.predict(sp_ev[\"Zev\"])\n    m = SVC(kernel=\"precomputed\", C=C, class_weight=\"balanced\").fit(sp_tr[\"K\"], y_tr)   # QSVM\n    return m.predict(sp_ev[\"Kev\"])\n\ndef tune_svm_C(sp_in, y_fit, y_val):\n    best = {}\n    for t in TASKS:\n        scores = {C: f1_score(y_val[t], svm_fit_predict(sp_in, y_fit[t], sp_in, C), average=\"macro\") for C in SVM_C_GRID}\n        best[t] = max(scores, key=scores.get)\n    return best","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:29:17.197784Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:29:17.198223Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:29:17.219694Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:29:17.198149Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:29:17.218383Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":9},{"id":"504861c7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Expériences (validation croisée stratifiée répétée)","metadata":{}},{"id":"fd628ff6","cell_type":"code","source":"def metrics(y, p):\n    return dict(accuracy=accuracy_score(y, p),\n                f1_macro=f1_score(y, p, average=\"macro\"),\n                qwk=cohen_kappa_score(y, p, weights=\"quadratic\"))\n\ndef model_name(family, space):\n    if space == \"Euclid\":\n        return {\"DBSCAN\": \"DBSCAN classique\", \"kNN\": \"kNN classique\", \"SVM\": \"SVM-RBF classique\"}[family]\n    a = space.split(\" \", 1)[1]\n    return {\"DBSCAN\": f\"Q-DBSCAN (a={a})\", \"kNN\": f\"kNN quantique (a={a})\", \"SVM\": f\"QSVM (a={a})\"}[family]\n\nrecords, OOF = [], {}\n\ndef log(exp, task, model, rep, fold, te, pred, **extra):\n    y = Y[task][te]\n    records.append(dict(experiment=exp, task=task, model=model, repeat=rep, fold=fold, **metrics(y, pred), **extra))\n    OOF.setdefault((exp, task, model, rep), np.full(len(y_multi), -1))[te] = pred\n\nsplits = list(RepeatedStratifiedKFold(n_splits=N_SPLITS, n_repeats=N_REPEATS, random_state=SEED)\n              .split(np.zeros(len(y_multi)), y_multi))\n\nt0 = time.time()\nfor kind, n_comp in EXPERIMENTS:\n    exp = f\"{kind.upper()}-{n_comp}\"\n    for fold_id, (tr, te) in enumerate(tqdm(splits, desc=exp)):\n        rep, fold = divmod(fold_id, N_SPLITS)\n\n        # --- split interne (train -> fit/val) pour choisir eps et C sans toucher au test ---\n        in_fit, in_val = train_test_split(np.arange(len(tr)), test_size=0.2,\n                                          stratify=y_multi[tr], random_state=SEED + fold_id)\n        itr, iva = tr[in_fit], tr[in_val]\n        inner, _     = build_spaces(itr, iva, kind, n_comp, SEED + fold_id)\n        outer, var   = build_spaces(tr,  te,  kind, n_comp, SEED + fold_id)\n        y_fit = {t: Y[t][itr] for t in TASKS}\n        y_val = {t: Y[t][iva] for t in TASKS}\n        y_tr  = {t: Y[t][tr]  for t in TASKS}\n\n        for sp_name in outer:\n            sp_in, sp_out = inner[sp_name], outer[sp_name]\n            q_best = tune_percentiles(sp_in[\"D\"], sp_in[\"Dev\"], y_fit, y_val)\n            C_best = tune_svm_C(sp_in, y_fit, y_val)\n            kd_out = kdist(sp_out[\"D\"])\n            cluster_cache = {}\n\n            for t, C in TASKS.items():\n                # ----- DBSCAN / Q-DBSCAN -----\n                q = q_best[t]\n                if q not in cluster_cache:\n                    cluster_cache[q] = DensityClassifierDBSCAN(np.percentile(kd_out, q)).cluster(sp_out[\"D\"])\n                clf = copy.copy(cluster_cache[q]).fit_labels(y_tr[t], C)\n                pred, cov = clf.predict(sp_out[\"Dev\"])\n                yt = Y[t][te]\n                log(exp, t, model_name(\"DBSCAN\", sp_name), rep, fold, te, pred,\n                    q=q, eps=clf.eps, n_clusters=clf.n_clusters_, noise_pct=100 * clf.noise_ratio_,\n                    coverage=cov.mean(), acc_covered=(accuracy_score(yt[cov], pred[cov]) if cov.any() else np.nan),\n                    ari=adjusted_rand_score(y_tr[t], clf.labels_), nmi=normalized_mutual_info_score(y_tr[t], clf.labels_),\n                    var_expl=var)\n                # ----- kNN (baseline) -----\n                log(exp, t, model_name(\"kNN\", sp_name), rep, fold, te,\n                    knn_predict(sp_out[\"Dev\"], y_tr[t], KNN_FALLBACK, C), var_expl=var)\n                # ----- SVM-RBF / QSVM (baseline) -----\n                log(exp, t, model_name(\"SVM\", sp_name), rep, fold, te,\n                    svm_fit_predict(sp_out, y_tr[t], sp_out, C_best[t]), C=C_best[t], var_expl=var)\n\nres = pd.DataFrame(records)\nprint(f\"Terminé en {(time.time() - t0) / 60:.1f} min — {len(res)} lignes de résultats\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T18:29:20.533165Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T18:29:20.533545Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T18:36:03.270707Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-08T18:29:20.533517Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T18:36:03.268888Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"PCA-4:   0%|          | 0/10 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"ca15eb67328f492393db41c0012e9a0e"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"PCA-8:   0%|          | 0/10 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"